rock and roll and football  super bowl weekend is officially upon us  and that means it is time for our annual  super bowl  city showdown as the buccaneers and  chiefs get ready to battle it out on the  field  we are looking at how their hometowns  stack up against one another  so we sent cbs this morning saturday  co-host michelle miller  to beautiful kansas city and jamie ukis  to tampa  which is already enjoying some home  field  since they are hosting this year's big  game  let's just start where it matters most  at quarterback this  is the grady goat foundation turn that g  into a b  and you've got brady goat as in tom  brady the greatest of all time  [Music]  brady is a 14-time pro bowl quarterback  a three-time league mvp  and of course the winner of six count em  six super bowl rings  sure but he did all that as a new  england patriot  and don't forget a baby goat is a kid  in kansas city's kid quarterback patrick  mahomes is just getting started  mahomes already has a ring from last  year's super bowl  and he's ready for more isn't that right  kids  [Music]  you know the tampa bay area is made up  of three cities tampa st  petersburg and clearwater this beautiful  cable state bridge  the sunshine skyway stretches across the  lower tampa bay  and spans three separate counties one  bridge  three counties how about this one street  two states both kansas city  over here you're in kansas city kansas  and over here you're in kansas city  missouri  or missouri depending on what part of  the state you're from  one city two states i got that beat  right now i'm standing in tampa in the  good old usa  but once i walk through this gate i'm in  cuba  this little space called jose marti park  was given to the cuban government in  1956  and the island nation still owns it  today and speaking of cuba  the cuban sandwich not invented in  havana  but right here in tampa fla  you want to talk about food really  kansas city  is all about the barbecue and kansas  speedway  is home to the american royal world  series of barbecue the world's  largest barbecue contest and this  i can smell that smoky goodness smoke in  the 1880s cigar makers moved into tampa  and started hand rolling the product  right here  hundreds of millions of cigars were  produced earning tampa the nickname  cigar city flip the calendar back and  the kansas city area was both free  and slave territory before the civil war  the underground railroad led people  across the missouri  to freedom in kansas kansas city is  where you'll find the world's  largest batman birdie also known as  the shuttlecock yeah michelle we heard  all about the biggest birdie last year  but when it comes to badminton  no one has tampa top the longest  badminton doubles marathon  ever took place between two tampa teams  and lasted a whopping 32 hours in 25  minutes  [Music]  another record tampa holds longest  continuous sidewalk  this is bay shore boulevard it runs four  and a half miles  that's a pretty long sidewalk for sure  but the sidewalks here in kansas city  are home to the largest pub crawls  ever in 2013 85 people took part and  more than 4 500 gallons of beer were  ordered  if you do the math that amounts to about  a gallon of beer per person  hey what are you doing  this one's for you mahomes dry january's  over  st petersburg is home to the world's  largest shuffleboard club  kansas city has a castle saint pete once  recorded 768 straight sunny  days invented in kansas city the bumper  sticker  the crock-pot the first scheduled  commercial airline flight took off from  this saint petersburg waterfront in  1914.  23 minutes later it landed here at the  entrance of the hillsborough river  in tampa not going to lie that's  impressive  but here's a first for kansas city best  shopping mall  in 1922 the country club plaza opened  and changed the way americans buy their  stuff  hey jamie this one's on cbs  make sure you pick me up a little  something but michelle while you shop  we really should be talking about sports  and tampa bay is on a roll  the tampa bay lightning won the stanley  cup the tampa bay rays made it to the  world series  and the tampa bay buccaneers are in the  super bowl  a a forget about those other sports  because we're talking about football so  good luck buccaneers brady or not  because the defending super bowl  champions  are from right here in kansas city  i think we need a slow clap here  well done michelle and jamie join us now  uh good morning to both of you  going into this did you have any  preconceptions jamie swag  yeah where is her swag yeah i know she's  got sunshine all around her that's what  she's working on i got this  what else do you need michelle i win big  time with this view  you went you went glamour girl no i i  gotta  do a shout out to my girl mari salon  she's a huge kansas city fan  because i am debt you got to show up and  we should point out that the snow is in  new jersey  not in kansas city so i was in new  jersey  what was the most surprising thing you  guys learned about your respective  cities  michelle you're up first  you you put me on the spot here the most  surprising  probably uh the shopping center yeah  the shopping center kind of surprised me  yeah yeah  i knew about slave free state i knew all  about that  of course i knew about the barbecue uh  but yeah  the the shuttlecock in the in the  shopping center didn't know  jamie what about you so i didn't realize  that cuban sandwich was actually  invented  here in tampa which they're delicious by  the way i've had one every single day  for lunch i'm hoping to be sick of them  by the time i get home because i don't  know how to make them myself  um but yeah the other surprising thing  is that when you do goat yoga  they leave hoof hoof hoof marks on your  back  uh they just healed today yeah i want to  know how long it took for you to get  that goat to stand on your back  there oh it takes seconds for the goat  to actually stand on your 